Package: tulpaGPU
Title: CUDA Backend for the 'tulpa' Bayesian Engine
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Runs the device operations of the 'tulpa' engine on an NVIDIA
    graphics processing unit: dense and sparse Cholesky factorizations,
    factorizations batched across the cells of a nested Laplace grid, basis
    products, observation scatter and fused likelihood kernels. The CUDA driver
    and the 'cuSOLVER', 'cuBLAS', 'NVRTC' and 'cuDSS' libraries are loaded at
    run time, so installing the package needs only a C++ compiler. Once loaded,
    'tulpa' sends each operation to the device when it lies above its measured
    size crossover, or always under control$device = "cuda".
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: C++17; at run time an NVIDIA driver and the CUDA 12 or 13
    runtime libraries
